J. Scanlon","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/AJS1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-21T11:02:57.7066667"},{"Id":"MRS1","Name":"Margaret R. Scarsdale","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MRS1","ResponseDate":"2023-03-06T10:27:09.1166667"},{"Id":"PSS1","Name":"Priscila S. Sousa","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/PSS1","ResponseDate":"2023-02-14T13:04:54.67"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H526/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Kushmerek of Fitchburg, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 526) of Michael P. Kushmerek and others for legislation to increase special education transportation reimbursements.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 5A of chapter 71B of the General Laws, as appearing the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by striking out, in subsection (c)  the words “and transportation”.\r\n\tSECTION 2: Section 5A of chapter 71B of the General Laws, as appearing the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “threshold.” , the following: Transportation costs shall be reimbursed at 90%.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}